    <string name="xa_use_desc">Only when a post can\'t be read publicly. Public posts never use your account.</string>
    <string name="xa_signout_title">Sign out of X?</string>
    <string name="xa_signout_message">The saved session is erased from this device and ended on X. Restricted posts can\'t be opened until you sign in again.</string>
    <string name="xa_sign_out">Sign out</string>
    <string name="xa_signed_out">Signed out</string>
    <string name="xa_security_title">How your sign-in is protected</string>
    <string name="xa_security_text">\u2022 You type your password on x.com itself; the app never sees it.\n\u2022 Only the session cookies are kept, encrypted with a key that stays in the Android Keystore.\n\u2022 They are sent only to x.com, never to the fallback service, and never written to logs.\n\u2022 Signing out erases them and the key. X limits what any account can see, so protected accounts you don\'t follow stay unavailable.</string>

